{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>All this.</b> He is still on the matter of warning the wise man not to disobey the king's command. It is: I observed, after I set my mind to it, a time when man ruled over man like himself, to his harm, and did evil to him. And this matter is joined to ki lechol chafeitz yesh eit umishpat [Ecclesiastes 8:6]."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Resolved the final Hebrew quotation from the verse context (8:6). The word ועשה read as continuing the observation."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:26.645930244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}